5.7
RQ7: Combined Results
We conducted an experiment to assess whether combining SBCR, IROutliner, and FMSA can achieve greater
code-size reduction than running any of these optimizations individually. To this end, we evaluated all six
permutations of the three passes across the entire LLVM Test Suite (2007 programs) using the pipeline in
Figure 7. We then selected the best-performing ordering and compared its results against applying each
optimization alone.
Discussion.
Table 5 summarizes the geometric means for each metric across the evaluated pass sequences.
The best ordering was IROutliner →SBCR →FMSA. This pipeline reduced the .text size in 86 benchmarks.
Among these, the geometric mean reduction in instruction count was −14.43%, outperforming each of the
three passes when used independently. It is worth noting that, if we restrict the comparison solely to .text
size reductions, FMSA achieves slightly higher average reductions; however, it does so over a much smaller
subset of programs (34 benchmarks).
