are unavailable.
By recording the phase lengths of individual cells using FUCCI techniques, it is
possible to obtain data on heterogeneity within the population. Here, we use the
coefficient of variation of phase lengths (CV), and the minimum length of each phase,
denoted by Ti in the PDE model (1)-(4). For a probability distribution with mean µ
