J
bf-CVAE Implementation and FVH-LT Results
J.1
bf-CVAE Implementation
We slightly modified the bfVAE structure and the FVH-LT procedure by incorporating the wine
quality score y as part of the input, i.e., x′ ←(x, y), to the encoder. We then appended y to the
learned latent space z i.e., z′ ←(z, y), before being passed to the decoder. We performed LT on y
with its range in the observed data while fixing the latent z at a randomly drawn sample from its
posterior distribution. Variances of the generated ˆx were computed.
