4.1. The Infinite-width Limit
In a suitable limit of infinite width, deep neural networks
initialized with standard scaling evolve linearly in their pa-
rameters (Hron et al., 2020; Jacot et al., 2018). The network
predictor f(X) converges to a kernel predictor defined by
the NTK. The kernel predictor takes the form of a weighted
sum over the training dataset {Xν}P
