For standard activation functions bounded by linear growth
(e.g., ReLU or GeLU), the dual activation integral is known
to be smooth and uniformly Lipschitz continuous with re-
spect to the input covariance entries (Schoenholz et al.,
2017). Consequently, the local error simply scales by a
bounded, architecture-dependent constant Lmlp such that
∥∆Σnext∥∞≤Lmlp ∥∆∥∞. This integration acts strictly
locally in the sequence dimension and inherently exhibits
zero dependence on T.
