Reason: GBM models assumes the constant volatility, which
fails to incorporate the real market dynamics and at the same
time the Heston models accommodate the real market scenario
such as stochastic volatility, allowing it to better match the
market prices. It was adjusted itself for the volatility skew
which is often observed in the options.


