B. Monte Carlo Method with Merton Jump Diffusion Model
In this method, the Merton Jump Diffusion model is inte-
grated into the original Monte Carlo method to further improve
the accuracy of the estimation of option prices. This model was
initially introduced [4] to overcome one of the limitations of
traditional methods in taking account for the large and sudden
price changes, this issue was found with MARA stock, whose
price fluctuation is high. The simulation of stock price can be
re-written as:
