The expected payoff is discounted back to the present by
utilizing the risk-free rate, defined as:
Option Price = e−rT × Average Payoff
(13)
Here e−rT is the discount factor and T is the expiration
time. The mean of all discounted payoffs over all simulated
paths is used to determine the final option price for a contract.
