and the theorem follows.
□
Remark 4.5. We can similarly treat the number of fringe trees that belong to some other given
subset of Tnκ, for example the number of fringe trees that are isomorphic to Tκ as unordered
rooted trees. (Note that a version of Lemma 3.13 holds for any subset of TnT , with the same
proof.) This gives straightforward generalizations of Theorems 4.2 and 4.4. We omit the details.
△
