where ai and τi are learnable parameters of the scaling law
estimated from small-scale pilot-runs (we provide details
in Section 9 of the Appendix.), and n denotes the number
of added samples [55]. Here, ai represents the asymptotic
improvement on the total utility U when sampling from
domain i, while τi governs the saturation rate, i.e., how
quickly the marginal benefit of adding data from the domain
decreases. Obtaining the scaling esimators is symbolically
