problem (2) yields a concave maximization problem that we
can compute and solve.
3.2.3. Scaling-Aware Iterative Data Collection by First-
Difference Steps
We propose an efficient algorithm to solve problem (2) by
allocating data samples one-by-one from the domain that
stands to give the highest marginal improvement to Umix
at any given time. Intuitively, this iterative adding of data
mimics a gradient-based approach of taking small steps to
optimize the data mixture.
