i=1 and
omit interaction and higher-order terms. Importantly, we
do not assume strict linear separability. Rather, we assume
that first-order cluster-wise scaling captures the dominant
variation in performance, while interaction terms contribute
residual approximation error.
To quantify the magnitude of the approximation error,
we compare the estimated EPDMS calculated by summing
cluster-wise scaling fits against the actual EPDMS obtained
with the MOSAIC data mixtures. As shown in Table 5, the
approximation overestimates performance by a modest mar-
gin (up to 1 EPMS), indicating that interaction terms are
present but negligible in this setting.
