it is larger than the threshold, the training process will diverge quickly. This phenomenon
is highly consistent with our analysis. To simplify the analysis, we omit the full terms of
the upper bound of β and select a constant bound in our theorems. In fact, the complete
upper bound of β is related to the learning rate η and the local interval K. However, in the
experiments, we find that a simple constant selection can offer high improvements.
